@format 1
@id media-preview.in-staged-workspace
@title In staged workspace
@section Media preview
@area In staged workspace
@entry staged-viewer-request
@summary Show why a selected-path request produced inside a temporary staged workspace does not start preview loading.
@related media-loading.in-staged-workspace, media-preview.common.viewer-gate
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag staging

@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer

[staged-viewer-request] Staged selected-path adapter calls viewer <input>
~ This starts when a temporary workspace selects a media file for preview.
[Technical explanation]
= Direct staged docket insertion can publish a first current path; a media-tab adapter that calls PViewerSourceOpen reaches the staged viewer.
> staged-command-state

[staged-command-state] Staged viewer command state <process>
~ This step handles staged viewer command state.
[Technical explanation]
- The temporary workspace is never attached as the active window workspace, so its viewer is not made command-active through PViewerCommandSet; PViewerSourceOpen therefore returns at the shared Viewer gate @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerCommandSet(...)
> staged-no-preview

[staged-no-preview] No staged preview load <output>
~ This path ends with no staged preview load.
[Technical explanation]
= The temporary workspace can contain loaded Files entries, but its inactive viewer does not begin backend preview loading.
